{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>However, My sabbaths you shall keep.</b> Scripture teaches you that the work of the Tabernacle does not set aside the Sabbath, and this is what it says: אך את שבתותי תשמרו — that is, even though you are engaged in the work of the Tabernacle, do not set aside the Sabbath on its account. And so the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: 'One might think that the building of the Temple sets aside the Sabbath — therefore it says (Leviticus 19:30): את שבתותי תשמורו ומקדשי תיראו.' According to this, the word אך is like אכן — that is to say, 'I have commanded you concerning the work of the Tabernacle; however, My sabbaths you shall keep,' and you shall not set aside the Sabbath on account of the work of the Tabernacle." "<b>And because</b> the word אך is a term of restriction, as the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: 'אכין ורקין מעוטין' — 'אך and רק are restrictive,' it appears to me to explain that it comes to restrict the observance of the Sabbath in the matter of the offerings, which would override the Sabbath, as the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: 'במועדו — and even on the Sabbath.' And similarly the way they expounded (ibid. 23) the אך in 'אך בעשור לחדש' etc. — Yom HaKippurim — which is also a restriction, coming to expound and restrict atonement to those who do not repent. And this is the same reason here: אך את שבתותי תשמרו — with respect to the work of the Tabernacle, and the word אך restricts the observance in the matter of the offerings. And the view of the Rabbis, of blessed memory, is that it comes to restrict the observance of the Sabbath in the case of danger to life (פקוח נפש), for so the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded in tractate Yoma, at the end of the chapter 'Yom HaKippurim': 'אך את שבתותי etc. — one might think for everything, that is, even for danger to life; Scripture says אך — to divide.'" "<b>And know</b> that the commandment of the Sabbath is the first commandment that was given to Israel before the giving of the Torah, and it is the root of faith, and it is weighed against all the commandments, all of them. And through the commandment of the Sabbath a person believes in the creation of the world ex nihilo, for it was created in six days and on the seventh day He rested. And the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: Jerusalem was not destroyed except because they profaned the Sabbath, as it is said (Ezekiel 22:26): ״ומשבתותי העלימו עיניהם ואחל בתוכם״. And so we find Jeremiah, who used to warn Israel about keeping the Sabbath, and would say that through the keeping of the Sabbath Jerusalem and the kingdom of the House of David would endure, and he prophesied to them that if they do not keep the Sabbath the city would be destroyed, as it says (Jeremiah 17:27): ״ואם לא תשמעו אלי לקדש את יום השבת ולבלתי שאת משא ובא בשערי ירושלים ביום השבת והצתי אש בשעריה ואכלה ארמנות ירושלים ולא תכבה״. And the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: if only Israel would keep even two Sabbaths, they would be immediately redeemed, as it is said (Isaiah 56:6–7): ״אשר ישמרו את שבתותי״, and immediately after it is written: ״והביאותים אל הר קדשי״. And they said further: anyone who keeps the Sabbath according to its law, even if he worships idols like the generation of Enosh — he is forgiven, as it is said (ibid.): ״אשרי אנוש יעשה זאת״ etc. ״שומר שבת מחללו״ — do not read מחללו but rather מחול לו — 'it is forgiven him.' <br><b>And that</b> which He mentioned 'My sabbaths' in the plural — by way of the plain sense (peshat), it is because there are many in the year." "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah:</b> את שבתותי תשמרו — זכור ושמור. And give your heart to El, how He said of both of them אות הוא — 'it is a sign' — in the singular, and did not say אות הם. And He explained through this that the Sabbath, which is Knesset Yisrael, is a sign upon the great Sabbath, and therefore He said that the Sabbath is 'a sign between Me and you, to know that I am YHWH.' And this is in the manner of what is said (Exodus 14:31): ״וירא ישראל את היד הגדולה״ — which is Knesset Yisrael, and it is the sign — and it says: ״וייראו העם את ה׳״ — for through their apprehension of the great hand, the people feared HaShem; it is as if He said that this is a sign of that. And I have already lengthened the discourse on the secret of the commandment of the Sabbath in the verse זכור את יום השבת, and there you will find the secret of the matter explained."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {1 "The lemma word ומפני appears to introduce the comment; the opening reads awkwardly as a lemma head. Translated hyper-literally as given."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:06:13.930339803Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}